chmod-lite oracle case: non-utf8

Isolates non-UTF-8 file names (bytes 0xFF and lone 0xE9, invalid UTF-8):
chmod-lite.py takes argv as raw bytes (surrogateescape) and re-execs
under PYTHONUTF8 when the locale encoding is not UTF-8, so such names
must be fixed like any other. The file inside the non-UTF-8 dir proves
the recursion descends through it.
If the native port regressed to decoding argv as UTF-8 str, it would
fail on or skip these entries instead of recording 0644/0755.

Run exactly as the unpack phase runs it (bin/phase-helpers.sh):
  cd <tree>
  find . -mindepth 1 -maxdepth 1 ! -type l \
    -exec <checkout>/bin/chmod-lite {} +
with PORTAGE_BIN_PATH=<checkout>/bin,
PORTAGE_PYM_PATH=<checkout>/lib, PORTAGE_PYTHON=/usr/bin/python.
File contents are empty (out of scope: only type/mode/path/target
are recorded); symlink modes are always ----.

Provenance (D4):
  portage-ref: portage-3.0.82.2
  portage-commit: 1d95fc2c552a2c7d347e54093fa0e5b172a57004 (3rdparty/repos.toml [portage] commit)
  python: Python 3.14.8 (/usr/bin/python)
  uid: 1000, umask: 0022
  staging: tmpfs bind mount (host filesystem rejects non-UTF-8 names)
  generator-locale: LC_ALL=unset LC_CTYPE=unset LANG=C.utf8 charmap=UTF-8
  date: 2026-10-08 (UTC day granularity; the only field that may change
    between regenerations)
  root-vs-user: identical
